#{[17592186430001 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430001 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111042" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430001 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430001 #edb/ref 1071 "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}{c}_{3},$ and ${c}_{1}$, ${c}_{2}$, and ${c}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430001 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6e653566-d375-5ee1-b745-3dfd829381b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430001 #edb/ref 1074 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -4 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -16 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(\\frac{7}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & -18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ -9{x}_{3}=-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}+3(2) & =-3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5-2(-3)-3(2) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=5\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{1}}+(-3)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{2}}+2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=5\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2=-30.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430002 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430002 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110965" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430002 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430002 #edb/ref 1071 "The matrix $K$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(K).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{k}_{1}+{x}_{2}{k}_{2},$ and ${k}_{1},$ ${k}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $K.$\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430002 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa3eae70-d536-57c6-818d-d88d2dc98925" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430002 #edb/ref 1074 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(K),$ we need to check if the equation $Kx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[K\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=3.$  \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(K).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
